= V2 architecture evaluation checkpoint =

This page is the evaluation surface for the first complete V1 → V2 maturation pass.

<blockquote>'''V1 gave us the imagination. V2 gives that imagination a coherent substrate.'''</blockquote>

The work at this checkpoint does not attempt to finish every future BITwiki capability. It finishes the '''evidence decomposition required to decide what should be built next without rewriting V1 or recreating its ambiguity.'''

== Governing sequence ==

<pre>
V1
→ preserve
→ understand
→ identify signal
→ mature primitive
→ enhance
→ integrate into V2
→ validate
</pre>

See [[BITwiki:V1 to V2 maturation]].

== What is complete at this checkpoint ==

=== V1 provenance preservation ===

The public V1 archive remains the historical evidence layer:

* 186 public pages;
* 606 revision bodies;
* 162 Main pages;
* exact source bodies, histories, category memberships, template callers and namespace evidence;
* design intent explicitly distinguished from implemented MediaWiki objects.

Nothing in this maturation pass rewrites the archive.

=== V1 implementation versus imagination ===

The architecture now explicitly distinguishes:

* '''design imagination''' — Charter/Manifesto/architecture/schema/ontology/template/research specifications and wanted capabilities;
* '''implementation reality''' — what MediaWiki actually contained and used.

A documented idea is evidence that BITwiki imagined a capability. It is not proof that the capability was deployed.

