=== Subject/composition disposition ===

The two first-class historical subject candidates are explicitly separated from reusable subject-bearing fragments.

* <code>Bioluminescent Organisms</code> — Concept-oriented Biology candidate assembled from historical subpages;
* <code>Fluorescent Coral Reefs</code> — Project/Implementation tension preserved for deliberate modeling rather than flattened.

Reusable fragments provide Concept, Method, Protocol and evidence/composition signals without forcing every fragment into a top-level page.

See [[BITwiki:V1 subject and composition migration]].

=== Ontology decomposition ===

The strongest V1 ontology signal is accepted at the architectural level:

{| class="wikitable"
! Question !! V2 primitive
|-
