The historical <code>Topic</code> label is not restored as one universal primitive because V1 used it for several of these jobs simultaneously.

=== Explicit semantic identity ===

<code>Template:Knowledge object</code> no longer invents semantic values when parameters are omitted.

Missing <code>entity_type</code>, <code>domain</code>, <code>status</code>, or <code>provenance</code> now produces no semantic assertion rather than silently creating <code>Concept</code>, <code>Unspecified</code>, <code>Established</code>, or <code>V2 public corpus</code>.

Repository validation requires all four fields on instantiated Knowledge objects and validates controlled values for current Entity type, Domain and Epistemic status vocabularies.

=== Machine validation and evidence generation ===

The pull-request gate now runs:

<pre>
python scripts/validate_v2.py
python scripts/inventory_corpus.py
python scripts/classify_v1_page_roles.py
python scripts/classify_v1_architecture_families.py
</pre>

Generated review evidence includes:

* <code>v2-validation.json</code>;
* <code>v2-corpus-inventory.json</code>;
* <code>v1-classification-usage.json</code>;
* <code>v1-page-role-matrix.json</code>;
* <code>v1-architecture-family-matrix.json</code>.

The classifiers fail on V1 snapshot drift, unresolved page roles, unmapped architecture sources, stale architecture mappings, invalid current Knowledge-object values, or missing required identity fields.

== What the evidence now says about V1 ==

V1 should not be understood as a failed 162-article encyclopedia.

It was predominantly an '''architecture laboratory and composition experiment''':

* 83 Main pages explored the system itself;
* 52 Main pages implemented reusable composition/Book Matter;
* 19 were navigation/interface surfaces;
* only two current historical artifacts behave like direct first-class subject objects under the conservative role test.

This explains why the conceptual system was far more sophisticated than the deployed subject corpus without treating that gap as failure.

== What is accepted ==

The following are strong enough to function as present architectural invariants unless later evidence overturns them:

# V2 is a maturation of V1, not a rewrite.
# Foundational voice and intellectual lineage must survive canonicalization.
# Namespace, Entity type, Domain, Category/navigation, Book Matter, epistemics, lifecycle and Relationships are independent jobs.
# Ontology is not navigation.
# Types are useful constructed/evolving lenses rather than a permanently closed metaphysical taxonomy.
# A canonical knowledge object normally has one primary modeled identity while secondary roles are represented through relationships/composition where cleaner.
# Schema grows from demonstrated content/query behavior rather than from historical property catalogs alone.
# Provenance must distinguish exact historical source, current canon, generated output and new connective text.
# Page role is not Entity type.
# Missing semantic identity must remain missing; the system must not manufacture certainty through defaults.

== What is a Candidate ==

These V1 ideas have enough durable signal and implementation evidence for a mature V2 form, but their final contract remains subject to implementation testing:

=== Book Matter ===
V1 directly implemented parent/subpage composition, generic transcludable sections, definition fragments, methodology fragments, protocol fragments and evidence summaries.

=== Transclusion ===
V1's two first-class historical subject pages actually assembled child content through transclusion. V2 should retain canonical-source reuse while avoiding arbitrary fragmentation.

=== Purposeful template families ===
V1 had implemented templates plus extensive template design writing. V2 should build small behavior-driven families from recurring callers, not recreate every historical/wanted template.

=== Portals and plural navigation ===
Portals, Categories, indices, outlines, semantic queries and graph views should be different views over shared semantic knowledge rather than competing taxonomies.

=== Human–AI knowledge production ===
BIThub live work, BITCORE cognition/orchestration, reusable artifacts, review, BITwiki durable knowledge and future reuse remain a durable lifecycle pattern independent of one model/runtime.

== What remains deliberately Research ==

These areas should not be treated as completed simply because V1 wrote sophisticated specifications for them:

=== Detailed epistemic/evidence object model ===
Current V2 has Epistemic status, confidence rationale, provenance, review/lifecycle separation and claim-validation grammar. The 16-source V1 epistemics family still requires mechanism-by-mechanism reconciliation before adding claim/evidence subobjects or more properties.

=== Universal confidence machinery ===
V1 explored tiers, scores, categories and confidence trails. V2 should preserve inspectable justification and contextual evidence without reintroducing a universal scalar merely because older pages contain numbers.

=== Property and relationship expansion ===
Current properties are a floor. V1 dictionaries/catalogs are research evidence. New properties require a recurring job, documented meaning, target/value constraints and validation.

=== Graph inference ===
Explicit semantic relations can generate graph views. Query paths must not silently become logical/causal inference.

=== Final Domain and Entity type vocabularies ===
The current V2 corpus contains twelve Concept exemplars plus two historical first-class subject candidates and reusable fragment signals. That is not enough evidence to freeze the complete future vocabulary.

=== Research/laboratory object model ===
Claims, patents, publications, datasets, experiments, labs, methods, implementations and projects are plausible mature objects, but the minimum useful research schema must be derived from actual corpus/workflow evidence.

== Intentional non-actions in this checkpoint ==

The pass intentionally does '''not''':

* publish reconstructed Bioluminescent Organisms or Fluorescent Coral Reefs as current factual canon before source review;
* add AI, Computer science, Knowledge representation, Governance, Economics or other new Domains merely because they seem useful;
* add Theory, Model, Framework, Software, Species, Algorithm or other specialized Entity types without repeated corpus pressure;
* restore V1 <code>Topic</code> as a universal class;
* import the full V1 Property Dictionary;
* recreate a single root taxonomy;
* adopt universal numeric confidence;
* treat old active/development labels as current facts;
* merge historical architecture branches by deletion;
* claim graph inference semantics that are not validated.

These are safeguards against premature architecture, not missing cleanup.

== Known next validation layers ==

The current validation gate now covers structure and explicit Knowledge-object identity. Future implementation phases should add tests when the corresponding capabilities become active, especially:

* relationship target resolution and documented relation vocabularies;
* controlled review/lifecycle values once those vocabularies are operationally fixed;
* canonical redirect/duplicate resolution;
* transclusion caller/cycle integrity;
* property domain/range constraints where meaningful;
* generated graph/query regression tests;
* research-object schema constraints after that model is accepted.

Do not build validators for semantics that have not yet been deliberately adopted.

== Evaluation questions ==

The human review at this checkpoint should focus on architecture rather than line editing:

# Does the V1→V2 maturation doctrine preserve the original ambition and crypto-punk/intellectual character?
# Does the role-before-ontology separation correctly explain the V1 corpus?
# Are the ten architecture families the right lenses for mining the 83 system sources?
# Is the Entity type / Domain / navigation / Book Matter / epistemics / lifecycle / Relationship decomposition coherent?
# Should Book Matter/transclusion/templates now proceed from Candidate to concrete implementation design?
# Are the two historical subject dispositions faithful without prematurely turning them into current factual canon?
# Which architecture family should receive the next deep maturation pass: epistemics/confidence, composition/templates, graph semantics, research/lab substrate, or navigation?

== Review state ==

'''This checkpoint is evaluation-ready, not merge-authorized.'''

The working branch should remain a draft review surface until the architecture is evaluated. Acceptance of this checkpoint can then determine which Candidate families move into executable V2 implementation.

